        "wb_port"
      ],
      "severity": "critical",
      "confidence": "unverified",
      "title": "Write acknowledge and read response complete in the same cycle on the one Wishbone ack line",
      "requirement": "One acknowledge per accepted beat (host_interface.interface_type = wishbone_pipelined). When a write acknowledge and a read response are due in the same cycle the port must hold one of them (a one-entry response or write-ack holding register) so each completes in its own cycle.",
      "spec_ref": "host_interface.interface_type",
      "expected": "One acknowledge per accepted beat (host_interface.interface_type = wishbone_pipelined). When a write acknowledge and a read response are due in the same cycle the port must hold one of them (a one-entry response or write-ack holding register) so each completes in its own cycle.",
      "actual": "cex at bound 24: $past(wb_cyc_i && wb_stb_i && !wb_stall_o && wb_we_i) && rsp_valid is reachable",
      "detector": "formal:jaspergold",
      "anchor": [
        {
          "file": "Frontend2/OutputFolders/PHASE1RTL/wb_port.sv",
          "signal": "wb_ack_o",
          "text": "assign wb_ack_o = wr_ack_r | rd_ack;",
          "line": 158
        },
        {
          "file": "Frontend2/OutputFolders/PHASE1RTL/wb_port.sv",
          "signal": "wr_ack_r",
          "text": "else        wr_ack_r <= wb_beat & wb_we_i;",
          "line": 155
        }
      ],
      "mechanism": "JasperGold counterexample 24 cycles from reset, engine L, no abstraction (cover c_HOST_001, a write beat accepted, reached at cycle 1). wb_port.sv: wr_ack_r <= wb_beat & wb_we_i (the write acknowledge, one cycle after the beat) and assign wb_ack_o = wr_ack_r | rd_ack with rd_ack = rsp_valid. A read response arriving the cycle after a write beat is accepted gives one wb_ack_o pulse for two completions; the host counts one acknowledge, waits for the other forever (a pipelined master) or mis-attributes the read data to the write (a classic one). Any legal host reaches it: issue a read, then present a write beat the cycle before the read data returns. Not seen in simulation on 2026-10-28 only because no sequence placed a write beat on that cycle (243 pipelined beats on path_07). SIMULATION WITNESS (2026-10-29, path_23_host_ack_collision, ack_collision.py): a read to an open row and a write beat accepted 41 cycles later (gap d = 40) -- the write acknowledge and the read response fall in the same cycle at t = 35.37 us; a_HOST_001 fires once, every request and response is conserved, and the host handshake stage counts 1 of 79 beats never acknowledged: the one ack pulse the two completions shared. [found on drop 99f72da45a32; awaiting formal re-prove on 56ca186bf893]",
      "paths": [
        "formal:chain_formal"
      ],
